**/target

# Cargo.lock is committed as of 2026-08-30, for the workspace root and for
# stet-wasm, which is a separate workspace (root Cargo.toml `exclude`).
# Pinning makes CI immune to upstream churn, lets a release be reconstructed
# from its tag, and turns the MSRV floor's held-back crates (hayro-jpeg2000,
# moxcms) into a visible diff instead of inferred resolver behaviour.
#
# Two locks stay ignored, for different reasons:
#
#   fuzz/ is excluded from the workspace and deliberately tracks a moving
#   nightly and a moving cargo-fuzz -- bit-rot detection is the whole point
#   of the weekly fuzz job, and pinning its dependencies would defeat it.
fuzz/Cargo.lock
#   crates/stet-tiny-skia/ IS a workspace member (`members = ["crates/*"]`),
#   so this lock is a stale artifact from building the vendored fork
#   standalone. Cargo never reads it; the root lock governs.
crates/stet-tiny-skia/Cargo.lock
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.png
!crates/stet-tiny-skia/tests/images/**/*.png
visual_tests_*
web/pkg/
crates/stet-wasm/pkg/
.test_stats.tmp
pdf_samples/
more_pdf_samples/

# AI-assistant files — local only, never committed
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Internal planning docs — kept locally, not tracked / never committed.
# Anything living under docs/ with the PUBLISH-*, PLAN-*, or TODO-* prefix
# stays out of the public repo. Generic project docs (ARCHITECTURE.md,
# DISPLAY-LIST.md, VIEWER-GUIDE.md) continue to track normally.
docs/PUBLISH-*.md
docs/PLAN-*.md
docs/TODO-*.md
# Integration test artifact — render_to_pdf writes here when output_path is unset
crates/stet/output.pdf

# Bulk PS corpus for gs differential testing (regenerable, lives on /data)
ps_corpus
ps_corpus/

# Fuzzing artefacts. Corpora are bulky and machine-generated, and are rebuilt
# from the in-tree sample sets by fuzz/seed-corpus.sh. Crash reproducers land
# in fuzz/artifacts — promote an interesting one into a real regression test
# rather than committing it here.
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
/docs/PLAN-SECURITY-HARDENING.md
